      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I found a workaround to make it reset back to \"rest\"-ish postion.\nIn your animation where you disable your physbone (If you don't have one that when it's disabled by default, make one), add 2 extra keyframes for the \"Phys Bone Enabled\" toggle.\nSet the toggle the very 1st keyframe(s) to off.\n2nd keyframe(s) to on.\nFinally, last keyframe(s) to off again.\nWhen you enable the physbones again, they reset back to rest position before simulating it's physics. So turning it off immediately after should set the bones to near \"rest\" position.\nHope this helps in the meantime!",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
